04:48.720 --> 04:49.100
[SPEAKER_04]: Lepers?

04:49.600 --> 04:50.801
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

04:51.481 --> 04:55.082
[SPEAKER_01]: You guys ever hear of the king of Jerusalem?

04:56.343 --> 04:56.623
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

04:57.663 --> 05:02.085
[SPEAKER_01]: Who was a leper and he had this mask on his face that was just totally silver?

05:02.765 --> 05:03.025
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

05:03.446 --> 05:03.626
[SPEAKER_01]: Right?

05:04.366 --> 05:04.546
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

05:04.666 --> 05:07.507
[SPEAKER_01]: He did that because he didn't want to scare people, right?

05:07.587 --> 05:15.170
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's basically what royalty would do during the Middle Ages if they got a horrible disfiguring disease, smallpox or whatever, right?

05:17.471 --> 05:17.851
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

05:19.342 --> 05:27.650
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, all of you know who Paul Rivero is, even though he's kind of a mysterious person in Lord Jeanne's court.

05:27.750 --> 05:37.039
[SPEAKER_01]: He is the son of Jeanne's sister, Lady Alleria.

05:38.197 --> 05:38.558
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

05:38.658 --> 05:40.399
[SPEAKER_01]: Who died many years ago.

05:42.742 --> 05:52.551
[SPEAKER_01]: And Paul Ribeiro never really shows his face, but the rumor is that he was horribly disfigured when he was a child by some weird accident.

05:52.791 --> 05:53.953
[SPEAKER_04]: And Merrick is with him?

05:55.114 --> 05:55.794
[SPEAKER_04]: Not Merrick.

05:56.095 --> 05:56.835
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh.

05:56.935 --> 06:01.940
[SPEAKER_04]: This weird looking elf, this like kind of tight-lipped,

06:03.095 --> 06:03.315
[SPEAKER_04]: Elf.

06:03.696 --> 06:03.996
[SPEAKER_04]: Okay.

06:04.276 --> 06:06.477
[SPEAKER_04]: Right, with a very, kind of a sour look on his face.

06:06.538 --> 06:10.701
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, not a joyous elf.

06:10.921 --> 06:12.982
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, should have been born a dark elf, but isn't one.

06:13.222 --> 06:13.623
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

06:15.138 --> 06:18.640
[SPEAKER_03]: And so how do I know these two, just from past adventures?

06:18.680 --> 06:20.601
[SPEAKER_04]: These guys are Marines.

06:20.701 --> 06:23.642
[SPEAKER_04]: And of course, you know Tyrus.

06:23.662 --> 06:25.383
[SPEAKER_04]: Tyrus is actually well known in the fleet.

06:25.423 --> 06:26.784
[SPEAKER_04]: He's kind of a boisterous guy.

06:27.284 --> 06:28.145
[SPEAKER_04]: Very charismatic.

06:28.205 --> 06:29.045
[SPEAKER_04]: Everybody loves him.

06:29.365 --> 06:30.126
[SPEAKER_04]: Tyrus?

06:30.506 --> 06:31.146
[SPEAKER_04]: Tyrus, yeah.

06:31.286 --> 06:31.986
[SPEAKER_02]: He's a big dude.

06:32.147 --> 06:32.827
[SPEAKER_04]: He's a big dude.

06:33.267 --> 06:45.198
[SPEAKER_01]: And Folsom is actually their companions because there's nothing that Tyrus likes more than to listen to Folsom play as Five because he's the best musician in the fleet, basically.

06:48.521 --> 06:51.424
[SPEAKER_01]: Not a very good fighter, but

06:54.612 --> 07:02.600
[SPEAKER_01]: Having somebody that lifts morale on a ship is probably more important most of the time anyway, so that's definitely what the deal is.

07:02.940 --> 07:09.846
[SPEAKER_04]: Anyway, as the two of you walk up, Tyrus' unit is the one that you're going to be attached to.

07:11.648 --> 07:18.435
